    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Wondrous Item, Artifact</em></p><p>This cubical box is 2 feet on each side. It seems to be made of oak bound in silver, and its surface is carved with marionettes and laughing children.</p><p>When a nonmagical item is placed inside and the lid is closed, a perfect copy of the item appears next to the box.</p><p><strong>Clone.</strong> As a Magic action, you can make the pantograph grow large enough for a Medium creature to crouch inside. You can return it to its normal size as a Magic action, harmlessly pushing anything that no longer fits into the nearest unoccupied space.</p><p>While a creature is inside, you can close the lid and sprinkle the pantograph with diamond dust worth at least 100 GP. The dust is consumed, and you cast @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplClone00000]{Clone} targeting the creature inside. When the spell’s casting time ends, the creature is harmlessly pushed out of the pantograph, and the lid can’t be opened for 120 days while the duplicate grows within. Once the clone has finished forming, it is harmlessly pushed out, and the pantograph returns to its original size. A clone made by the pantograph doesn’t need to be kept in a vessel and endures indefinitely while inert.</p><p><strong>Destroying the Pantograph.</strong> If it doesn’t hold a clone, the pantograph is destroyed after being submerged in a bog in the Feywild for 999 years.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
